  ('being-a-good-teammate', 198, 'Text a teammate after a tough game to say you liked how they kept their head up.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 199, 'Name the feeling to yourself, like "frustrated" or "embarrassed," before you respond in a tense moment.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 200, 'Ask your team which holidays and days matter to them, so coverage can be planned fairly and kindly.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 201, 'Nod or say "got it" when someone gives you instructions, so they know the message arrived.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 202, 'Arrive a few minutes early for your shift so the person leaving can head home on time.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 203, 'Look for the person standing alone at a volunteer event and invite them into your group''s conversation.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 204, 'Correct a small mistake you made in a shared document, and leave a short note saying you fixed it.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 205, 'Keep a meeting you lead to the time you promised, and end a minute early if you can.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 206, 'Avoid typing in all capital letters in chat today, and use a plain sentence instead.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 207, 'Step in for the one task you can handle when you see a coworker juggling phones and customers at once.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 208, 'Sign the group card for a colleague with a specific memory, not just your name.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 209, 'Open a critique by asking, "Can I offer a thought on that?" and wait for a yes.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 210, 'Celebrate a teammate''s news from outside work, like a new home or a finished class, with a warm message.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 211, 'Share hard news with a teammate in person or on a call, not in a hurried text.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 212, 'Tidy the comments you left in a shared document, deleting notes that no longer help anyone.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 213, 'Offer to pair with a new coworker on one task this afternoon so they feel less alone.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 214, 'Restate the other person''s point in your own words before you share your disagreement with it.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 215, 'Learn how to say good morning in a teammate''s first language, and try it gently.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 216, 'Tell people when you have finished something they were waiting on, instead of letting them discover it.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 217, 'Let the person in your study group with the soonest exam choose the first topic tonight.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 218, 'Nominate a teammate for any recognition your workplace or school offers, with a few honest lines.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 219, 'Consider whether a disagreement will still matter next season before deciding how hard to push.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 220, 'Lower your voice in a shared space where others are concentrating, or step out to take a call.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 221, 'Tell everyone affected at once when a plan changes, instead of a few people at a time.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 222, 'Return the shared laptop or tablet fully charged, ready for the next person who needs it.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 223, 'Praise effort out loud during an autumn fundraiser setup, naming who carried what.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 224, 'Set a time to talk through a disagreement properly, instead of hashing it out in a busy hallway.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 225, 'Hold back from correcting a teammate''s small wording in front of others, and mention it later only if it matters.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 226, 'Lend your class notes to a classmate who was absent, with a line pointing out the most important part.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 227, 'Admit one thing you cannot finish by the deadline and ask the group how to share it out fairly.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 228, 'At your morning standup, ask the team who deserves a shout out, then give it.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 229, 'Apologize for interrupting someone in a meeting, and invite them to finish their thought.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 230, 'Bundle a few small questions for a busy teammate into one message instead of interrupting them several times.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 231, 'Use suggestion mode when you edit a teammate''s shared document, so they stay in charge of their own words.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 232, 'Do the small, dull part of your task first today, the piece others are waiting on.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 233, 'Thank someone for asking a question others were too shy to ask.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 234, 'Admit when you don''t know an answer at the register, and say you''ll find someone who does.'),
