  ('being-a-good-teammate', 245, 'When snow or ice slows everyone down, send a kind "take your time, stay safe" message to anyone running late.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 246, 'Set your chat status to show when you are focused or away, so teammates know when to expect a reply.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 247, 'Close the loop on work you handed off by checking the person who took it has everything they need.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 248, 'Share a teammate''s good work in a wider channel, after checking they are comfortable with it.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 249, 'Look at criticism you received again an hour later, and pick out the one useful part to act on.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 250, 'In spring, invite a teammate to spend their break with you on a short walk around the block.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 251, 'Draw the team''s plan on a whiteboard or shared screen so everyone can see the same picture.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 252, 'Take a turn washing the team''s practice bibs, or offer to join the laundry rotation.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 253, 'Message a remote coworker to ask how things are going, and thank them for one thing they finished.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 254, 'Accept an apology from a teammate simply, with "Thank you, we''re good."'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 255, 'Answer a newer person''s question patiently, even if you have answered it before.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 256, 'In a spring team meeting, ask the person leading it what a good result looks like before the group starts planning.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 257, 'Ask a teammate before you jump in on their task, so your help fits what they actually need.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 258, 'Celebrate a coworker''s work anniversary with a short, warm message about what they bring.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 259, 'Let a teammate know kindly that a joke landed badly, in private and with no audience.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 260, 'Rest properly on your day off, and let the team handle things without checking in.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 261, 'Leave a handoff note at the end of your shift listing anything the next person needs to know.'),
