  ('being-a-good-teammate', 362, 'Thank yourself for carrying your fair share today, then rest without checking messages again.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 363, 'Close your day by thinking of one teammate you appreciated and how you will tell them tomorrow.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 364, 'Forgive yourself tonight for one awkward moment with a teammate, the way you would forgive a friend.'),
  ('being-a-good-teammate', 365, 'Hum a favorite song on your way to a shift or class so you arrive in a friendly mood.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 1, 'Find any deck of cards in your home today and set it somewhere you will see it, like the kitchen table.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 2, 'Tell someone at home about a game that made you laugh as a child, and describe the place where you used to play it.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 3, 'Step outside with someone you love and toss a soft ball back and forth a few times, just for the fun of hearing each other laugh.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 4, 'Make up a tongue twister with your own name in it, and say it three times fast for someone at home.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 5, 'Ask someone near you if they would like to play a quick round of tic tac toe, and smile whatever happens.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 6, 'Ask someone you live with to play one quick hand of go fish, and let the silly requests make you both smile.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 7, 'Dust off a board game you have not touched in a while and ask someone at home to play a round.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 8, 'Invite a child or a neighbor to a slow game of tag in a fenced yard, where everyone walks quickly instead of running.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 9, 'Think of an animal and let a friend ask up to twenty yes or no questions over morning coffee.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 10, 'Make a small trophy from foil for the silliest moment of the game, and award it to whoever made everyone laugh the most.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 11, 'Tuck a small deck of cards into your bag or coat pocket so a game is ready whenever a chance appears.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 12, 'Spread a jigsaw puzzle on the kitchen table and invite anyone who passes by to add a piece.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 13, 'Draw a hopscotch grid with sidewalk chalk on a quiet patio and take turns hopping through it, wobbles and all.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 14, 'Take turns telling a bedtime story one sentence at a time, and see where the silliest twist leads.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 15, 'Laugh out loud the next time you make a silly mistake in a game, and say, "Well, that was a good one."'),
  ('playing-games-together', 16, 'Play a round of war with a child after dinner, and cheer just as loudly for their cards as for your own.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 17, 'Set up a checkers board after dinner and offer a game to whoever is nearby.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 18, 'Gather a few friends at the park on a spring evening for an easy game of bocce, and cheer for every good roll, yours or theirs.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 19, 'Act out a favorite movie title in a quick game of charades with family after supper.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 20, 'Pick team names before the game that make everyone laugh, and use them in every cheer.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 21, 'Teach a friend a simple card game you learned as a kid, and tell them who first taught it to you.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 22, 'Choose a regular evening for family game night and write it on the shared calendar.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 23, 'Toss a flying disc with a coworker on a lawn during lunch, keeping the throws gentle enough that anyone can catch them.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 24, 'Pass the time on a train ride by playing the alphabet game with signs you see out the window.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 25, 'Explain the rules of a favorite card game to a beginner one step at a time, then play an open hand round so they can learn.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 26, 'Sit beside your partner and play solitaire side by side, trading little comments as your cards turn up.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 27, 'Set up a game of ludo with your family, and cheer each time someone brings a piece safely home.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 28, 'Set up a round of hide and seek in the backyard at dusk with your family, choosing hiding spots that stay inside the yard.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 29, 'Hum the opening of a song you love and let someone at home guess what it is.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 30, 'Pause before your turn and let the quietest player at the table go first.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 31, 'Roll two dice with a family member and take turns making up a silly rule for each number that appears.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 32, 'Draw a nine men''s morris board on a sheet of paper, use buttons as the pieces, and learn this very old game with a friend.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 33, 'Write a short scavenger hunt list for a park path: a red leaf, a round stone, a singing bird, a cloud shaped like something.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 34, 'Ask a coworker a would you rather question at lunch, and share your own answer too.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 35, 'Mirror a partner''s slow movements in a mirror game, then switch leaders and try not to giggle.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 36, 'Set out a box of dominoes on a rainy afternoon and invite whoever is home to line up a few tiles with you.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 37, 'Look up your local library''s game night and note when the next one is.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 38, 'Mark a circle in the dirt with a stick and play a round of marbles with a child, cheering when one taps another out of the ring.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 39, 'Share the newspaper crossword with a partner over coffee, each filling in the clues you know.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 40, 'Invent a brand new game with a sock, a hat and a few simple rules, and name it together.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 41, 'Call a grandparent and ask which card game they loved most when they were young.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 42, 'Meet a friend at a board game cafe and try a game neither of you has played before.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 43, 'After a fresh snowfall, build a snowman target in the yard and take turns lobbing soft snowballs at it, never at people.'),
  ('playing-games-together', 44, 'Phone a faraway friend and play the dictionary game, reading out a rare word while they guess what it means.'),
